From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:40:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] function runner: validate detached shadow snapshot
 retention

A shared timestamped index reader does not pin persistence history. The authoritative result passes retention validation, but a detached verifier may continue reading after that check. Retain the admitted timestamp and validator independently of the primary publication sender, then validate after each shadow completes before accepting comparison evidence.

An unavailable snapshot produces the existing invalid-shadow terminal, never agreement or semantic divergence. Validation remains inside the bounded background deadline and does not delay, retract, or replace the primary response. Keeping validation ownership separate preserves prompt channel closure when the caller is cancelled.

Document the snapshot/read-set distinction and retention behavior. Add delayed-verifier tests for both execution directions, valid and expired snapshots, and keep the caller-cancellation regression. The new test fails without the final checks; all 69 function-runner tests pass with them.
